# wren_fixpoint_by_value:
# Turing's fixed point combinator with the self-application under a λ, the
# form a strict reading ends on: fixpoint is generic Θ, Θ = A A with
# A = λx.λf. f (x x f), and this define is B B with B = λx.λf. f (λv. x x f v),
# equal to Θ by η under λ. The typed member of wren_typed_bindings spells fixpoint this
# way.
. (λtuple. tuple λ. (λx f. f λv. x x f v) λx f. f λv. x x f v)
λ wren_fixpoint_by_value
# wren_typed_branch:
# The marker of a typed branch: β-equal to the identity, applied to the
# typed member of a choice that a wren_typed_block lemma makes. Its body is
# the identity's η expansion, not in normal form, so that no other define and
# no program's identity shares its handle (a condition of 2026-11-03: hash
# consing would make the identity's applications this
# marker's applications). noinline, so the e-graph reads it as a leaf.
. (λtuple. tuple λx. (λy. y) x)
λ wren_typed_branch
# wren_typed_zero:
# The canonical binary zero under its type: binary_zero filtered by
# binary_set true, the representation binary_natural at true
# (binary_prolog_backend). wren_typed_block, the typed branch of a binding
# of binary_zero.
. (λtuple. tuple (binary_zero ∥ binary_set true))
λ wren_typed_zero
# wren_typed_even:
# binary_even under its type: a positive binary natural to a positive one
# (binary_set false; 2h is canonical for a positive h only).
. (λtuple. tuple λ. arrow (binary_set false) (binary_set false) binary_even)
λ wren_typed_even
# wren_typed_odd:
# binary_odd under its type: a canonical binary natural to a positive one.
. (λtuple. tuple λ. arrow (binary_set true) (binary_set false) binary_odd)
λ wren_typed_odd
